in order to be able to go and find the right solution.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.880
I could take the existing implementation

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.760
and put it in the supporting information

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:26.840
but I think it's just cleaner to tell it to go

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.160
and look at the existing implementation first.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.400
So I've now told it in the start of the steps to complete,

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.880
look at the existing implementations of functions

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.640
and tools in the correct directory,

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.160
load them into your context window, be very specific.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:40.080
So let's take this entire prompt

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.000
and stick it in the chat window.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.640
We're actually going to use this chat here.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:45.520
We're going to go all the way up to the top

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:48.400
and we're essentially just going to paste it in here instead.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.120
So we're going to override the previous chat message

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.720
and then just go back.

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:56.200
This means that all of the code that we had before

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.600
essentially gets removed.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.160
So we don't no longer have that dodgy action stuff.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.880
You can see it's all been removed

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:03.520
if I move my face.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.720
Ooh, I just go over here for a sec.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.320
All the action stuff has been removed

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.800
from functions and tools.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.520
We can see now that thanks to our explicit instruction,

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.680
it's going first, let's look at the existing

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:15.360
GitHub functions and tools.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.560
Let me check the implementation

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.480
of one of the existing function files.

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.480
Let me check how these things are exposed to tools.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.080
It's reading the correct files,

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.560
loading them into its context window.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.000
Okay, we now have an actions file

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:28.880
that looks very much like the other actions that we had here.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.760
Again, it's relying on its training data,

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.800
really spitting out these OctoKit functions.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:36.440
And here we can see the actions are much more like it.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.040
Just like this issues file here

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.760
where we have registered issues tools,

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.320
we have an actions thing here

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.960
that says register action tools.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.440
And so the previous hallucination,

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.360
I mean, was that our fault?

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:47.520
Was it the LLM's fault?

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.400
Maybe the LLM should have been smart enough

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:50.680
to understand that it should have looked

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:51.920
in those files first.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.480
But honestly, I put this down to me

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.680
not thinking ahead, not understanding

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.960
what the LLM's context was supposed to be.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:00.120
It had to have those files in context.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.560
If it didn't have the files in context,

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:03.000
it had no idea what it was going to do.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.160
So explicitly telling it,

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.640
load those files into context

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.840
and essentially copy them is the way to go.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.600
So there we go, in a series of five prompts,

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:14.000
we have a bunch of stuff that can look like an MCP server.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.240
We have a bunch of folders

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:17.200
that will allow us to add features here

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.760
where the LLM understands what it's supposed to do.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.040
We have all the infrastructure needed

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:23.160
to run this as an MCP server locally.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:24.360
And we've done this with prompts

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.800
that use a three section heading kind of thing.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:30.240
They explain the problem that we're supposed to be solving.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.720
They give the LLM any supporting information it needs,

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.040
like external resources.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.600
And then you have the explicit steps to complete,

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:37.760
which is really important.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:38.520
I hope you enjoyed this.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.600
I definitely enjoyed making this

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:40.640
and I'll be back with more.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:41.640
See you very soon.

